---
/**
 * /workflows-page/json/ — the JSON live preview: edit a blueprint, validate
 * it, and paint it with @texuli/player at the untrusted tier, in the browser.
 */
import JsonPreviewApp from '../../../components/workflows-site/json/JsonPreviewApp.svelte';
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="JSON live preview"
  description="Edit a Texuli blueprint as JSON, see the validator's diagnostics with their JSON paths, and watch @texuli/player paint it at the untrusted tier. Everything runs in your browser."
>
  <div class="json-page" data-tx-json-page="">
    <header class="json-page__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">@texuli/player · spec 0.3.0</p>
      <h1>JSON live preview</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Texuli builds interfaces from validated JSON. Edit a blueprint on the left: it is
        checked as you type, and only a blueprint with no errors is painted by the real player,
        at the untrusted tier an agent's output gets. Nothing you type leaves the browser.
      </p>
    </header>

    <JsonPreviewApp client:visible />

    <section class="json-page__notes" aria-labelledby="json-page-how">
      <h2 id="json-page-how">How the preview works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Parse.</strong> The text must be JSON; a syntax error is reported with its line
          and column.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Validate.</strong> The same checks the player runs: the local-state
          declarations, the player's binding checks and <code>validateDraft</code> from
          <code>@texuli/catalog/validate</code> with the player catalog (component ids, prop schemas,
          bindings, events and closed actions, block schemas, composition grammar and the untrusted
          URL policy). Each diagnostic lists its code, its message and its JSON path.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Paint or refuse.</strong> With no errors, <code>&lt;Player&gt;</code> paints the
          blueprint at the <code>untrusted</code> tier and validates it again. With any error the
          preview is cleared, never left showing an older result, and the status reads
          “Not rendered”.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="json-page-status">What is in development</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The player's runtime for the spec 0.3.0 interaction fields (local state in the envelope,
          <code>on</code> actions, <code>reorder</code> and workflow graphs) is in development and
          first published in <code>@texuli/player</code> <code>0.4.0</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>@texuli/workflows</code>, which paints the <code>workflow-graph</code> node, is in
          development and on npm as <code>0.5.0</code>; the player's <code>workflow-graph</code>
          painter that uses it ships from the player's <code>0.4.0</code> release. The preview shows graphs
          read-only.
        </li>
        <li>
          This page does not run the spec's own structural validator
          (<code>validateBlueprint</code> from <code>@texuli/spec</code>); the player's checks
          above decide what paints.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .json-page {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--tx-foreground);
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    color: var(--tx-foreground);
  }
  .lead {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    max-inline-size: 44rem;
    color: var(--tx-foreground);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }
  .json-page__notes {
    max-inline-size: 48rem;
    color: var(--tx-foreground);
  }
  .json-page__notes h2 {
    margin: 1rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }
  .json-page__notes ol,
  .json-page__notes ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
